{# The initialiser of one `<data>` in the form the engine policy's `defineData` takes it: the lowered
   `expr`, the lowered inline text with the string it spells as its last reading (W3C SCXML B.2), or
   none. Written where the document's data is declared at load (`script_engine.swift.jinja2`) and where
   a state with late binding declares its own on its first entry (`entry_exit_actions.swift.jinja2`), so
   the two cannot read one `<data>` two ways.

   It lives beside the Swift templates and not in the shared `_macros/`: the directory is the C++
   backend's by the ownership rule (`Language::owns_template`), so an expression site written there
   would be counted as C++'s. #}
{% macro data_source(var) -%}
{%- if var.expr -%}as: "{{ var.expr | to_lua_expr | escape_swift }}"
{%- elif var.content -%}as: "{{ var.content | to_lua_data_content | escape_swift }}", orText: "{{ var.content | normalize_ws | escape_swift }}"
{%- else -%}as: nil
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}
